.omo
.reference
# Root-anchored: matches only the repo's dev dependency tree, NOT the
# vendored `dist/node_modules/typescript/` that `scripts/post-bundle.mjs`
# copies in for the bundled CLI. The leading slash is load-bearing — an
# unanchored `node_modules/` would silently ignore any nested copy too
# (PR #209 ci failure: tarball shipped without the runtime, `--version`
# blew up with `ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND`).
/node_modules/
# Local review/eval artifacts produced by manual runs, e2e harnesses, and
# the post-release canary. None of these ever need to land in git — every
# path under artifacts/ is regenerated on demand by the script that wrote
# it (see scripts/ci-smoke.mjs SCENARIOS table + test/post-release/).
# The leading slash anchors to the repo root so a future `artifacts/`
# subdir under a different package (e.g. examples/*/artifacts/) does NOT
# inherit this ignore rule.
# Note: even though `artifacts/scratch/` and `artifacts/manual/` are
# covered below, the parent `artifacts/` MUST also be ignored — git only
# ignores a path when at least one matching rule applies, and without the
# parent rule the bare top-level directory shows as untracked.
/artifacts/
artifacts/scratch/
artifacts/manual/
.env
.playwright-mcp/
.layout-viewer-build/
*.tsbuildinfo
build/
*.png

# ncc bundle staging directory — created by `npm run bundle` before
# `scripts/post-bundle.mjs` renames the cli bundle and rmSync's the tmp dir.
# If a build aborts before post-bundle runs, this leaks untracked content.
dist-tmp/

# OS / editor scratch (Windows, macOS, vim/emacs leaks).
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Tooling-generated logs that should never be committed.
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# Coverage output from vitest --coverage (not currently enabled, but
# safe to declare so the first person who turns it on doesn't accidentally
# commit coverage/).
coverage/
.vitest-cache/

# Personal env / version files that some contributors drop at repo root.
# (.env is already ignored; these are sibling files for direnv/asdf/pyenv.)
.envrc
.env.*
!.env.example
.tool-versions
.python-version
umactually-review.json
.umactually*
